#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Canonical links, social cards, structured data, sitemap and robots.txt.

    python3 tools/build_seo.py            # write everything
    python3 tools/build_seo.py --check    # fail if anything is stale

Every indexable page carries one managed block in the head, between

    <!-- SEO · generated by tools/build_seo.py -->
    <!-- /SEO -->

holding the canonical link, the Open Graph and Twitter cards, and a
JSON-LD graph. Nothing outside the markers is touched, so the block can
be rebuilt after any other tool has written the page. The facts in the
graph are read from the page itself: the title, the description, the
date and venue line of a concert, the programme list, the performers.
Nothing is invented here. A street address or a ticket price only
appears if it is in VENUES or TICKETS below, where every entry was
checked against the venue or the ticket seller.

Run it last:

    python3 tools/build_news.py && python3 tools/build_presenters.py \\
      && python3 tools/build_seo.py
"""

